{"name":"Cotton Cardigan","hex":"#7596b8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cotton","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fibrous substance:\n A soft, fibrous, usually white substance consisting of fine hairs, especially the substance around the seeds of a plant of genus Gossypium.\n Any similar soft, fibrous, white substance of fine hairs, of any origin.","A soft, fibrous, usually white substance consisting of fine hairs, especially the substance around the seeds of a plant of genus Gossypium."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of cotton."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cotton"},{"term":"cardigan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of sweater or jumper that fastens up the front with buttons or a zipper, usually machine- or hand-knitted from wool."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cardigan"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cardigan (sweater)","blocks":[{"text":"A cardigan is a type of knitted garment that has an open front and is worn like a jacket."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/NMA.0038588%2C_Fashion_Photo_by_Erik_Holm%C3%A9n_1947.jpg/330px-NMA.0038588%2C_Fashion_Photo_by_Erik_Holm%C3%A9n_1947.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cardigan_(sweater)"},{"title":"Cardigan (UK Parliament constituency)","blocks":[{"text":"The Cardigan District of Boroughs was a parliamentary constituency in Wales which returned one Member of Parliament (MP) to the House of Commons of the Parliament of the United Kingdom and its predecessors, from 1542 until it was abolished for the 1885 general election. The borough constituency comprised the four towns of Cardigan, Aberystwyth, Lampeter and Adpar - geographically separated from each other but all within the county of Cardiganshire."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cardigan_(UK_Parliament_constituency)"},{"title":"Cotton","blocks":[{"